    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "亲爱的弟兄啊，我们既有这等应许，就当洁净自己，除去身体、灵魂一切的污秽，敬畏　神，得以成圣。",
      "en": "Therefore, since we have these promises, dear friends, let us cleanse ourselves[NOTE:1] from everything that could defile the body[NOTE:2] and the spirit, and thus accomplish[NOTE:3] holiness out of reverence for God.[NOTE:4]",
      "notes": [
        "Or “purify ourselves.”",
        "Grk “from every defilement of the flesh.”",
        "Grk “accomplishing.” The participle has been translated as a finite verb due to considerations of contemporary English style, and “thus” has been supplied to indicate that it represents a result of the previous cleansing.",
        "Grk “in the fear of God.”"
      ],
